C# is a statically-typed language, which means that the data type of a variable is known at compile time. This helps to catch type-related errors early in the development process.

C# supports object-oriented programming (OOP) concepts such as encapsulation, inheritance, and polymorphism. It also supports functional programming concepts such as lambda expressions and delegates.

